From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:28:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: state the power plan and RAM as pre-registered
 conditions, not per-launch receipts

The R14 check (FABLE-53-LOW-R14-CHECK.md, FIX-1): Balanced power plan and
RAM 48 GB (32 + 16) appear in no AB.json header and no per-launch receipt;
they are declared in PREREG-r8-integration.md only, and the R8 report says
not to credit them. The CHANGELOG conditions line and F-18 now say so, and
name what IS receipted per launch (free RAM before and after, the
load-governor guard, the RAM-floor wait). F-18 also gains "context 8192",
which the CHANGELOG line already carried (check residual).

Docs only.

Origin: lane-213 R17C docs fix (HQ seat-53 amendment, R14 check FIX-1)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documentation wording; no engine behaviour changed by this commit.
Lane: lane-213
---
 CHANGELOG.md     | 6 ++++--
 docs/FINDINGS.md | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
